{"id":"lisbon-dakar","title":"Lisbon to Dakar","who":"Classic route · overland by adventure motorcycle","when":"November to March","vehicle":"Adventure motorcycle, 3–4 weeks","kind":"moto","color":"#9a3412","summary":"The old rally's spirit on public roads: from Lisbon to the Strait of Gibraltar, through Morocco and down the long Atlantic desert road, across Mauritania's Sahara and the Senegal river to Saint-Louis and Dakar. Borders take hours: Mauritania now needs an e-visa arranged in advance (since 2025), and the Diama crossing into Senegal needs planning.","sources":[{"label":"Sahara Overland: Mauritania (updated May 2026)","url":"https://sahara-overland.com/mauritania/"},{"label":"Ducati: route to Dakar with the Multistrada V4 Rally","url":"https://www.ducati.com/au/en/stories/travel/route-to-dakar-with-the-multistrada-v4-rally"},{"label":"JB's Trails: riding a motorcycle across Mauritania","url":"https://jbstrails.com/?p=24857"}],"approximate":"The main towns on the coastal route; the roads are the router's choice.","km":4184,"bbox":[-17.4476,14.6934,-5.605,38.7103],"stops":[{"name":"Lisbon","place":"Lisbon, Portugal","at":[38.7078,-9.1366],"text":"The start, by the Tagus.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Lisboa_-_Portugal_%2852597836992%29.jpg/500px-Lisboa_-_Portugal_%2852597836992%29.jpg","page":"Lisbon","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lisboa_-_Portugal_%2852597836992%29.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Tarifa","place":"Tarifa, Spain","at":[36.0129,-5.605],"text":"Through the Alentejo and Andalusia to the southern tip of Europe."},{"name":"Tangier","place":"Tangier, Morocco","at":[35.7695,-5.8045],"text":"A short ferry over the Strait into Africa.","by":"ferry","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Tanger_cor.jpg/500px-Tanger_cor.jpg","page":"Tangier","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tanger_cor.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Marrakech","place":"Marrakech, Morocco","at":[31.6258,-7.9892],"text":"South past Rabat to the red city.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Marrakech%2C_Morocco_%285421595453%29_%285%29.jpg/500px-Marrakech%2C_Morocco_%285421595453%29_%285%29.jpg","page":"Marrakesh","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marrakech%2C_Morocco_%285421595453%29_%285%29.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Agadir","place":"Agadir, Morocco","at":[30.4205,-9.5839],"text":"Over the Atlas to the Atlantic surf coast.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/South_view_sea_side_from_Kasbah_of_Agadir_Oufella_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-South_view_sea_side_from_Kasbah_of_Agadir_Oufella_%28cropped%29.jpg","page":"Agadir","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:South_view_sea_side_from_Kasbah_of_Agadir_Oufella_%28cropped%29.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Tan-Tan","place":"Tan-Tan, Morocco","at":[28.4376,-11.0987],"text":"Into the desert; the road follows the ocean cliffs for days.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Tan_tan.jpg/500px-Tan_tan.jpg","page":"Tan-Tan","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tan_tan.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Laâyoune","place":"Laayoune","at":[27.1545,-13.1954],"text":"The main town of Western Sahara, police checkpoints on the way.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/El_Aai%C3%BAn-La%C3%A2youne_Collage.png/500px-El_Aai%C3%BAn-La%C3%A2youne_Collage.png","page":"Laayoune","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:El_Aai%C3%BAn-La%C3%A2youne_Collage.png","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Dakhla","place":"Dakhla","at":[23.6941,-15.9431],"text":"A lagoon peninsula famous for kitesurfing, the last big stop before the border."},{"name":"Nouadhibou","place":"Nouadhibou, Mauritania","at":[20.9127,-17.0503],"text":"Across the no-man's-land at Guerguerat into Mauritania.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Nouadhibou_port.jpg/500px-Nouadhibou_port.jpg","page":"Nouadhibou","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nouadhibou_port.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Nouakchott","place":"Nouakchott, Mauritania","at":[18.0792,-15.978],"text":"Desert tarmac with fuel only every few hundred kilometres.","source":{"label":"JB's Trails: across Mauritania","url":"https://jbstrails.com/?p=24857"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Nouakchott.jpg/500px-Nouakchott.jpg","page":"Nouakchott","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nouakchott.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Saint-Louis","place":"Saint-Louis, Senegal","at":[16.028,-16.5049],"text":"By the Diama dam and the Djoudj bird park into Senegal's old colonial capital.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Island_of_Saint-Louis-113799.jpg/500px-Island_of_Saint-Louis-113799.jpg","page":"Saint-Louis, Senegal","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Island_of_Saint-Louis-113799.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Dakar","place":"Dakar, Senegal","at":[14.6934,-17.4479],"text":"The finish at Africa's westernmost city; many ride on to Lac Rose, the old rally finish.","source":{"label":"Ducati: route to Dakar","url":"https://www.ducati.com/au/en/stories/travel/route-to-dakar-with-the-multistrada-v4-rally"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Dakar-Ind%C3%A9pendance.jpg/500px-Dakar-Ind%C3%A9pendance.jpg","page":"Dakar","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dakar-Ind%C3%A9pendance.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence